---
/** How it works: one request's path drawn as nested boxes (you, Clank, the gateway, the models), with three notes. */
---

<section class="section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2 id="how-title">One gateway between your agents and every model.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Clank runs OpenCode, an open-source coding agent, in a Docker workspace per folder. Each request it makes passes
        through Clank's gateway, to your GPU or to a cloud provider with your key.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <figure class="nest" aria-label="Clank's layers, nested: you, Clank, its gateway, and the models behind it">
        <div class="n n-you">
          <p class="n-head"><b>You</b><span>the console · VS Code · iPhone, coming</span></p>
          <div class="n n-clank">
            <p class="n-head"><b>Clank</b><span>the Monitor · the Guide · Flows · records</span></p>
            <div class="n n-agent">
              <p class="n-head"><b>The agent</b><span>OpenCode, in a Docker workspace per folder</span></p>
              <p class="n-body">Sees one folder. Reaches only Clank; git or the web only if you grant it.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="n-pass" aria-hidden="true"><span class="n-line"></span><span>every request</span><span class="n-down"></span><span class="n-line"></span></p>
            <div class="n n-gw">
              <p class="n-head"><b>The gateway</b><span>records, guards and meters every request</span></p>
              <ul class="chips" aria-label="What the gateway does">
                <li>records</li>
                <li>loop guard</li>
                <li>context margin</li>
                <li>census</li>
                <li>consent</li>
                <li>cost</li>
                <li>hold</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="targets">
                <div class="n n-gpu">
                  <b>Your GPU</b>
                  <span>any open model, on llama.cpp or KVMem</span>
                </div>
                <p class="or">and/or</p>
                <div class="n n-cloud">
                  <b>A cloud API key</b>
                  <span>OpenRouter, after your yes</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <ol class="notes">
        <li>
          <h3>One service, three ways in</h3>
          <p>The console, Clank's VS Code window and, soon, the iPhone app. A question waits in each, and an answer in one shows in all.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>A sandbox per folder</h3>
          <p>Each folder gets its own workspace. The agent sees that folder and reaches only Clank.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Swap the model, keep the rest</h3>
          <p>Local or cloud, the model sits behind the same gateway. Switching is one key; the agent and its folder stay as they are.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="go"><a class="more" href="/features#gateway">One request, end to end</a></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .how {
    margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 4fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 4vw, 64px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .nest {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .n {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--c);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: clamp(12px, 1.6vw, 18px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    background: var(--bg-n, transparent);
  }

  .n-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 2px 14px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .n-head b {
    color: var(--c);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .n-head span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .n-you {
    --c: var(--purple);
  }

  .n-clank {
    --c: var(--orange);
    --bg-n: rgba(26, 27, 38, 0.6);
  }

  .n-agent {
    --c: var(--line-strong);
    --bg-n: var(--surface);
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .n-agent .n-head b {
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .n-body {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .n-gw {
    --c: var(--yellow);
    --bg-n: var(--surface);
  }

  .n-pass {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: -4px 0;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .n-line {
    flex: 1;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--line-strong);
  }

  .n-down {
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    margin-left: -4px;
    border-left: 4.5px solid transparent;
    border-right: 4.5px solid transparent;
    border-top: 6px solid var(--faint);
  }

  .chips {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .chips li {
    padding: 1px 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .targets {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .n-gpu,
  .n-cloud {
    gap: 4px;
    background: var(--well);
  }

  .n-gpu {
    --c: var(--teal);
  }

  .n-cloud {
    --c: var(--blue);
    border-style: dashed;
  }

  .n-gpu b,
  .n-cloud b {
    color: var(--c);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .n-gpu span,
  .n-cloud span {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .or {
    align-self: center;
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .notes {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  .notes li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    padding-left: 18px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .notes h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .notes p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .notes li.go {
    border-left: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .how {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .notes {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
      gap: 24px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .targets {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .or {
      justify-self: center;
    }

    .nest {
      font-size: 0.8rem;
    }
  }
</style>
